  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening resilience and sustainable development in the English- and Dutch-speaking Caribbean SIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIDS in the English- and Dutch-speaking Caribbean face growing vulnerabilities linked to climate change, natural hazards, environmental degradation, and economic shocks. These challenges threaten ecosystems, livelihoods, cultural heritage, and sustainable development.
This initiative aims to strengthen resilience through integrated and community-based approaches that promote environmental sustainability and sustainable development. Key activities include supporting the implementation of UNESCO&#x2019;s Island Watch programme, promoting sustainable waste reduction in a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, and developing an intersectoral project proposal aligned with UNESCO&#x2019;s Six Transformative Actions (Accelerators).
The initiative will foster partnerships, knowledge-sharing, and inclusive participation, particularly among local communities, women, and youth, to enhance resilience and support sustainable development across Caribbean SIDS.</narrative>
  </description>
